## Problem

The GitHub Actions pipeline was a bottleneck, sometimes taking 3 to 4 hours. My team reviewed each workflow and found the unit tests were the slowest step.

## Root cause

The codebase used path aliases that resolved to barrel index files. Each import pulled in an entire folder, so every unit test loaded far more code than it needed.

## Fixes

- **Direct imports.** Replaced the aliased barrel imports with imports of specific submodules, cutting what each test loaded.
- **Affected-tests script.** A shell script detected which files a change touched and ran only the unit tests they affected, instead of the full suite.

## Results

CI dropped from about 3–4 hours to between 5 and 30 minutes.

## Also built

An internal tool that linked each design to its Jira tickets, so designers could see what each design was for and whom to contact when they changed it.
